 "codes_note": "Keys are PB2002 codes. NNR-MORVEL56 Table 1 writes the 25 MORVEL plates in lowercase and Bird's 31 plates in uppercase; lowercase codes are uppercased here except three that differ from PB2002: nb Nubia -> AF (PB2002 'Africa'), sm Somalia -> SO, yz Yangtze -> YA. Uppercase NB is North Bismarck (Bird), not Nubia. sc = SC Scotia and su = SU Sunda match PB2002; sr is Sur (part of PB2002 SA), not Scotia. Four MORVEL plates are not separate plates in PB2002 and carry pb2002:false: CP Capricorn and MQ Macquarie (inside PB2002 AU), LW Lwandle (inside PB2002 AF/SO), SR Sur (inside PB2002 SA). All 52 PB2002 codes have a pole. morvel_abbr is the code as printed in Table 1; omega_95 is the 95% confidence limit on omega.",
